Next step
Use the test findings to refine the final solution, identify remaining fixes or limitations, and prepare the last implementation and reflection phase so I can explain what the project achieved, what changed, and what I would improve next.




Phase 6: Implement





Objective
In Implement I refine and finalise the template system in the custom CMS by implementing the most important findings from the usability testing, so that a stable and approved version is available as a complete product for real campaigns. The focus is on translating evidence from Test into concrete improvements in templates, components and configuration flow and on delivering clear documentation and recommendations.





Linked research question(s)
SQ4 – Implementation and refinement in the CMS (final integration).
SQ5 – Impact and future improvement directions.
SQ6 – Potential AI support for configuration (recommendations).
Implement completes SQ4 by integrating the tested solution into the CMS in its refined and approved form, concludes SQ5 by reflecting on the impact of the final system and its remaining limitations, and closes SQ6 by turning AI findings into practical recommendations rather than further prototype work.




Approach and methods
I use the findings from the usability testing and consolidated report as the basis for the final implementation round. I review the feedback, decide which issues must be fixed before approval, apply the changes in the CMS and in the design documentation, and validate the final result with stakeholders. This phase is therefore both practical and reflective: I improve the working system, document the final decisions, and prepare the project for handover and final evaluation.




